{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqf624kvlk9","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Preference gate: heuristic-first, learned shadow auto-promotes when it beats heuristic","summary":"User decision (2026-06-15): to stop the dispatcher asking the user for preferences so often, add a second gate that predicts the answer from stored preference notes and only escalates via request_guidance when genuinely needed — structurally the same binary gate as the context-need gate (lib/context-gate.js), applied to the ask-vs-predict surface. Phasing the user chose: (1) ship a HEURISTIC ask-gate now (mirror context-gate four-guard pattern), logging every decision to a new .graph/ask-journal.jsonl; (2) train a LEARNED classifier on that journal running in SHADOW mode; (3) AUTO-PROMOTE the learned gate over the heuristic the moment it beats the heuristic on holdout over the same rows (no manual promotion). Hard override: irreversible/outward-facing/high-impact/scope-expansion/repeated-failure decisions ALWAYS ask, never predict. Note: an automated promotion gate already exists for the edge classifier (d08e0c33/6, agreement_rate>threshold) — T3 builds on that template rather than inventing the comparator. Decomposed as tasks 0b5a907e.../1 (heuristic+journal), /2 (dispatcher consults gate before request_guidance + preference-note convention category:\"preference\"), /3 (learned + auto-promote).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T12:05:20.431Z","vec":[-0.10580964386463165,-0.03169432282447815,-0.04939305782318115,0.06821124255657196,0.01857893541455269,-0.060014743357896805,0.01009965967386961,0.022101690992712975,-0.044131338596343994,0.05456375703215599,-0.009587772190570831,-0.04516264423727989,-0.024238819256424904,0.040949732065200806,0.048787813633680344,0.036036502569913864,0.032128140330314636,-0.02934229001402855,-0.10740029066801071,-0.03946050629019737,0.09234724938869476,-0.021363776177167892,0.02470136247575283,-0.027869172394275665,-0.075873069465160